8, mol_003 -> mol_009, mol_001 (Ammonia-driven conversion of the cyanohydrin reservoir) [Surface]\n  - rxn_005: mol_002, mol_005, mol_001 -> mol_008, mol_003, mol_006 (Sulfide-driven photoreductive homologation of HCN to glycolonitrile) [Surface]\n  - rxn_006: mol_009, mol_001 -> mol_010 (Acid-catalyzed aminoacetonitrile hydration to glycinamide) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_007: mol_010, mol_001 -> mol_011, mol_003 (Glycinamide hydrolysis to glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_008: mol_009, mol_012 -> mol_013 (Bucherer-Bergs capture of aminoacetonitrile as hydantoin) [Surface]\n  - rxn_009: mol_013, mol_001 -> mol_014 (Hydantoin ring opening to hydantoic acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_010: mol_014, mol_001 -> mol_011, mol_003, mol_012 (Hydantoic acid hydrolysis and decarbamoylation) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_011: mol_015, mol_003, mol_016 -> mol_011, mol_012 (CO-driven reductive amination of glyoxylate on mixed nickel-iron sulfides) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_012: mol_015, mol_003, mol_017 -> mol_011, mol_001 (Hydrogen-driven reductive amination of glyoxylate on a nickel-rich alloy) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_013: mol_015, mol_018 -> mol_019, mol_001 (Formation of glyoxylic acid oxime) [Surface]\n  - rxn_014: mol_019, mol_017 -> mol_011, mol_001 (Hydrogenation and N-O bond cleavage of glyoxylic acid oxime) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_015: mol_002 -> mol_020 (HCN oligomerization through a transient aminomalononitrile pool) [Surface]\n  - rxn_016: mol_020, mol_001 -> mol_021, mol_003 (Hydrolysis of aminomalononitrile to aminomalonic acid) [Hydrothermal]\n  - rxn_017: mol_021 -> mol_011, mol_012 (Decarboxylation of aminomalonic acid to glycine) [Hydrothermal]\n\nPATHWAYS (10):\n  - P1: Formaldehyde-imine Strecker route with direct hydrolysis (4 steps)\n  - P2: Formaldehyde-cyanohydrin Strecker route with direct hydrolysis (4 steps)\n  - P3: Photochemical HCN entry with direct Strecker hydrolysis (4 steps)\n  - P4: Imine-entry Strecker route through a hydantoin reservoir (5 steps)\n  - P5: